            "text": "\"Tommy went out at seven in his cowboy hat and never came back. They searched the woods and the river all night. I lit the first pumpkin of the evening for him and swore it would burn until he came home. My grandmother used to say the dead come home at midnight on All Hallows' Eve. So I wait for midnight. But the clock never reaches it now, and he never comes.\" She is not a monster. She is a mother keeping a promise, and her candle holds the night one minute short of the hour when her son could come home.\n",
